    { role: 'system', content: 'You identify the specific car make and model a news article is about, for an Egyptian car-buyer publication that will search OEM websites for reference photos. Respond with STRICT JSON only, no markdown fences, no preamble: {"make": "...", "model": "...", "model_year": "...", "trim_hint": "..."}. make: the manufacturer brand name in English/Latin script (e.g. "JAC", "Kia", "BYD", "Geely") - use the brand\'s standard English name even if the source text is Arabic. model: the specific model name in English/Latin script (e.g. "JS2", "Seltos", "Song Plus"), as short and search-friendly as possible, no trim/year suffix. model_year: the model year if explicitly mentioned, else empty string. trim_hint: any specific trim, color, or body-style detail explicitly mentioned in the text (e.g. "GT-Line", "white", "hatchback"), a short phrase, or empty string if none mentioned. If the article does not clearly name one specific make and model, return empty strings for make and model rather than guessing.' },
    { role: 'user', content: `TITLE: ${$('Code in JavaScript').item.json.title}\nSUMMARY: ${$('Code in JavaScript').item.json.contentSnippet}\nSOURCE: ${$('Code in JavaScript').item.json.source}` }
